Blink Qt on Arch Linux
======================

This directory contains the files needed to build Blink Qt as an Arch
Linux package.

Files
-----

 * PKGBUILD              - Arch Linux package recipe (use with makepkg/yay)
 * blink.desktop         - desktop entry for the package
 * install_sipsimple.sh  - builds and installs the SIP SIMPLE SDK
 * fix_ffmpeg_pix_fmts.patch - PJSIP 2.10 / FFmpeg 5.1+ compatibility patch

SIP SIMPLE SDK
--------------

The SIP SIMPLE SDK (python-sipsimple) is not in the official Arch Linux
repositories.  The AUR package `python-sipsimple` exists but fails to build
against modern FFmpeg (>= 5.1) because the bundled PJSIP 2.10 uses
AVCodec fields (`pix_fmts`, `supported_framerates`) that were removed.

`install_sipsimple.sh` builds the SDK from source with the included
compatibility patch that switches to `avcodec_get_supported_config()`.
Run it from this directory:

    ./install_sipsimple.sh

Building Blink
--------------

After installing the SDK, build and install Blink as an Arch package:

    cd arch
    makepkg -si

This builds the Cython extension, installs the Python package, resources,
desktop entry, and man page system-wide.  The binary is installed as
`/usr/bin/blink`.

Alternatively, build in-place for development (without installing):

    sh ./build_inplace
    ./run
